#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""One-off script to write the 5 pilot template translations (NL source +
FR translation + adaptation notes) to translated_templates_fr_pilot.jsonl.

v2: incorporates the adversarial review's findings plus a systemic issue
found while fixing it -- derender_templates.py can only recover SPANNED
(scored) slots, so unscored narrative fields (PATIENT_NOUN_MARKED,
PRONOUN_SUBJ, HONORIFIC -- none of which appear in MERGED/SPLIT/FLAT9)
never left a span to mask back. The first-pass translation therefore
accidentally froze these as literal gendered text tied to whichever one
case built the original Dutch corpus, which would silently render the
wrong gender roughly half the time on future re-renders. Fixed by manually
re-slotting every such occurrence, and by restructuring sentences that had
a French gender-agreement trap the first pass didn't fully account for
(leading Le/La + a MARKED noun, and passive-voice past participles that
agree with a fronted gendered subject) -- same class of fix as the
DEMO_TEMPLATE "Le/la {PATIENT_NOUN_MARKED}" bug in pii_table_fr.py.
Not part of the reusable pipeline; a scratch build script."""

